SUMMARY:Maz Jobrani LIVE at San Jose Improv
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nMaz Jobrani is one of the most celebrated comedians in the world\, known for his sharp wit\, cross-cultural storytelling\, and ability to connect with audiences from all walks of life. Born in Iran and raised in the United States\, Maz has built a career on finding the humor in the immigrant experience\, family life\, and the absurdities of modern society. \nHe is a founding member of the legendary Axis of Evil Comedy Tour\, which aired on Comedy Central\, and has released multiple acclaimed specials including Immigrant on Netflix (filmed at the Kennedy Center) and his most recent special The Birds and the Bees\, available on YouTube. Maz has appeared on The Late Show with Stephen Colbert\, The Late Late Show with James Corden\, and NPR’s Wait Wait Don’t Tell Me. \nHis comedy is warm\, intelligent\, and universally relatable — whether you’re laughing at his parenting stories\, his observations about American culture\, or his hilarious takes on international travel. Maz is a master storyteller who leaves audiences in stitches from start to finish. \nEvent Details\nDate: Friday\, July 24\, 2026 \nShow Time: 7:30 PM (Doors open approximately 6:30 PM) \nVenue: San Jose Improv\, 62 S Second St\, San Jose\, CA 95113 \nAge Restrictions: 18+ (valid ID required). Content may include adult themes. \nShow Duration: Approximately 90 minutes to 2 hours. \nAbout the Venue\nThe San Jose Improv is the Bay Area’s premier stand-up comedy club\, located in the heart of downtown San Jose at 62 S Second St. This intimate venue seats approximately 250-300 guests in a classic comedy club layout\, with tables and chairs arranged for an up-close\, personal experience with the performer. \nThe club features a full bar and food menu\, so you can enjoy drinks and bites throughout the show. The intimate setting means every seat is a great seat — you’ll feel like Maz is performing just for you. The venue has a lively\, energetic atmosphere that makes every show feel like a special event. \nParking is available in nearby garages and street parking throughout downtown San Jose. The venue is also accessible via VTA light rail and is a short walk from the San Jose Diridon Station. Arrive early to grab a drink and settle in before the show begins. \nWhat to Expect\nThis is a full-length solo stand-up performance by Maz Jobrani\, featuring his latest material. Expect a night of sharp\, culturally rich comedy that blends personal stories with broader social observations. Maz is known for his energetic stage presence and his ability to work the crowd\, making each show feel unique and spontaneous. \nThe show typically runs 90 minutes to two hours\, with Maz performing his full set. There may be an opening act to warm up the crowd before Maz takes the stage. This is an intimate club setting\, so the laughs feel personal and the energy is electric. \nWhether you’re a longtime fan or discovering Maz for the first time\, this is a night of comedy you won’t soon forget. Grab your tickets before they sell out — the San Jose Improv fills up fast for headliners of this caliber! \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $43 – $100+ (fees may apply) \nTickets are available through Ticketmaster/TicketWeb (official) and VividSeats (resale). Both options are backed by buyer guarantees. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/maz-jobrani-live-at-san-jose-improv/
LOCATION:San Jose Improv\, 62 S Second St\, San Jose\, California\, 95113\, United States
